nalism"},{"text":"Investigative Journalism"},{"text":"Digital Journalism"},{"text":"Data Journalism"},{"text":"Media & Communication"},{"text":"International Journalism"},{"text":"Science Communication"},{"text":"Political Communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Countries commonly considered include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Ireland"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Before applying, verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accreditation"},{"text":"Programme curriculum"},{"text":"Internship opportunities"},{"text":"Journalism-industry access"},{"text":"Visa/work rules"},{"text":"Tuition and living costs"},{"text":"Post-study work options"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A realistic newsroom progression can look like:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Journalism Intern","Trainee/Junior Reporter","Reporter","Senior Reporter","Correspondent / Specialist Reporter","Senior Correspondent","Chief Correspondent / Bureau Chief","News Editor / Special Projects Editor","Managing Editor / Editorial Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact titles vary substantially between organisations."},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Reporter","Investigative Journalist","Investigations Editor"]},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["Reporter","Data Journalist","Data Journalism Editor"]},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["Reporter","Technology Reporter","Technology Editor"]},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["Reporter","Video Journalist","Multimedia Producer","Executive Producer"]}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Paths","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A. Investigative Journalism"},{"type":"p","text":"Best for students who enjoy:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Deep research"},{"text":"Documents"},{"text":"Public records"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"t