 newsrooms."}]},{"heading":"AI & Future of Reporting — 2030–2045","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will significantly change reporting workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"AI will increasingly assist with"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Document summarisation"},{"text":"Large-document analysis"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Pattern detection"},{"text":"Search and research"},{"text":"Archive analysis"},{"text":"Headline suggestions"},{"text":"Personalisation"},{"text":"Video clipping"},{"text":"Caption generation"},{"text":"Monitoring large information streams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"But human reporters remain important for"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Source relationships"},{"text":"Investigative reporting"},{"text":"Field reporting"},{"text":"Accountability journalism"},{"text":"Context"},{"text":"Editorial judgement"},{"text":"Ethical decisions"},{"text":"Sensitive interviews"},{"text":"Verification"},{"text":"Public-interest reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The future reporter should therefore become:"},{"type":"p","text":"A journalist who can investigate, analyse data, use AI responsibly and explain complex information clearly."}]},{"heading":"AI-Era Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Traditional Journalism","Modern Journalism"],"rows":[[{"text":"News writing"},{"text":"AI-assisted editorial workflow"}],[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Digital/source verification"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"OSINT + AI research"}],[{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Computational/mobile photography"}],[{"text":"Reporting"},{"text":"Data-driven reporting"}],[{"text":"Newspaper publishing"},{"text":"Multi-platform publishing"}],[{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"AI-assisted editing + human review"}],[{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Data journalism"}],[{"text":"TV reporting"},{"text":"Multimedia storytelling"}],[{"text":"Audience understanding"},{"text":"Analytics + audience intelligence"}]]}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an excellent candidate should have:"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BA Journalism & Mass Communication"},{"text":"Strong understanding of journalism ethics"},{"text":"Media law fundamentals"},{"text":"Strong current-affairs knowledge"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Reporting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Fact-checking"},{"text":"Source development"},{"text":"News writing"},{"text":"Investigative research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"WordPress/CMS"},{"text":"SEO fundamentals"},{"text":"Social media"},{"text":"Mobile journalism"},{"text":"Video editing"},{"text":"Photography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Basic Python/R"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Document analysis"},{"text":"AI verification"},{"text":"Understanding hallucinations and source reliability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Ideally:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"25–40 written stories"},{"text":"3–5 substantial feature/investigative stories"},{"text":"2–3 video reports"},{"text":"1 data-journalism project"},{"text":"1 specialist beat portfolio"},{"text":"At least 1–2 newsroom internships"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Quality matters more than simply reaching the numbers."}]},{"heading":"Alternative Career Paths","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BA Journalism & Mass Communication graduate can also move into:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"News Editor"},{"text":"Copy Editor"},{"text":"Content Writer"},{"text":"Content Strategist"},{"text":"Digital Content Producer"},{"text":"News Researcher"},{"text":"Fact Checker"},{"text":"Social Media Manager"},{"text":"Digital Marketing Executive"},{"text":"SEO Content Specialist"},{"text":"Corporate Communications Executive"},{"text":"Public Relations Executive"},{"text":"Public Affairs Associate"},{"text":"Communications Specialist"},{"text":"Podcast Producer"},{"text":"Video Journalist"},{"text":"Documentary Researcher"},{"text":"Script Writer"},{"text":"Brand Journalist"},{"text":"Data Journalist"},{"text":"Media Analyst"},{"text":"Communications Consultant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Practical Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Journalism & Mass Communication","Year 1: Journalism + writing + interviewing + current affairs","Year 2: Field reporting + digital journalism + video + photography","Year 3: Choose a beat — Technology / Business / Politics / Sports / Science / Investigative / Data","Learn Excel + SQL + basic Python/R + data visualisation","Build 25–40 quality portfolio pieces","Complete 1–2 newsroom/media internships","Learn AI-assisted research, transcription and verification workflows","Apply for Reporter / Junior Reporter / Digital Reporter / Multimedia Journalist roles","Reporter","Senior Reporter / Specialist Reporter","Correspondent / Investigative Journalist / Data Journalist","Senior Correspondent / Editor","News Editor / Bureau Chief / Editorial Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Final recommendation"},{"type":"p","text":"For a student choosing Reporter as a career, the strongest 2026 profile is no longer simply:"},{"type":"h","text":"Journalism degree + good writing"},{"type":"p","text":"It is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Journalism","reporting","fact-checking","multimedia","data","AI literacy","specialist domain knowledge","a verifiable portfolio."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This gives the graduate both a direct route into reporting and strong alternatives across the wider digital media industry."}]}]}